+/*
+ * 0160: AppleARMBacklight for the Note 10 5G (d1x): the service iOS's brightness system looks for, so the
+ * Settings / Control Center slider has somewhere to go.
+ *
+ * Ported from guacamole 0197 (research/ext/ios-guacamole/xnu/patches/0197-guacamole-applearmbacklight.patch):
+ * CoreBrightness (in backboardd) finds the built-in display's brightness control with
+ * IOServiceGetMatchingServices({IOPropertyMatch: {backlight-control: true}}), checks IOObjectConformsTo(service,
+ * "AppleARMBacklight") and builds its display modules on it (guacamole NOTES.md, "0197 AppleARMBacklight so
+ * CoreBrightness starts"). With none it logs "Built in display/backlight driver has not been found.", which is the
+ * state of our kernel before this patch.
+ *
+ * The service carries the iPhone X's /device-tree/backlight node (DBVMin 139 / DBVMax 2047, marketing table,
+ * restriction curves; taken unchanged from 0197), backlight-control = true, IODisplayParameters
+ * { brightness = { min 0, max 65536, value } } and a user client that accepts every selector.
+ *
+ * Boot-arg d2sbl (default 0):
+ *   0  not registered (start() fails): no change from 0158.
+ *   1  registered; each brightness level iOS asks for is logged "D1X BL: ..." and kept as a property
+ *      (IODisplayParameters, d1x-bl-level, d1x-bl-percent) so userland or a later patch can read it back.
+ *      The panel is NOT touched.
+ *   2  reserved for panel writes, NOT implemented: behaves as 1 and says so once. Why: on this panel
+ *      (s6e3fa7_davinci1_a3_s0, research/cruel/exynos9820-d1x_kor_23.dts:7096) Samsung's set-brightness
+ *      sequence is not a DCS 0x51 write. research/cruel/fa7_davinci1.h:1190-1205 (set_bl_cmdtbl) sends, under
+ *      the 0xF0 0x5A 0x5A key (:534), a 34-byte gamma packet 0xCA (:625), AOR 0xB1 (:640), ELVSS 0xB5 (:641),
+ *      ACL, IRC 0xB8, then 0xF7 0x03 (:674). The per-level gamma table is empty in the source (:87) and filled
+ *      at run time from the panel's own MTP calibration (init_gamma_table, :488), so there is no fixed byte
+ *      sequence to send per level. DSIM0 is at 0x19080000 (research/cruel/exynos9825.dts:6776-6778), but its
+ *      command FIFO registers are not in our research tree. Writing guessed values could leave the panel dark
+ *      or overdriven, so d2sbl=2 waits for the DSIM driver + dimming data (see the patch notes).
+ */
